  clock: 4  # 34e1
  nonce: '34e1'  # 34e1
  message: "Fixed in PR #2183. extract_doc_comment reads a comment's markers from the comment itself and returns the first line that documents: a line with no letter, a tag line, a shebang on line one, a modeline, an encoding or a licence line are passed over, and a line that only restates the declaration is passed over when a describing line follows. BEHAVIOUR: the dashed-line and shebang summaries seen on kserve, lazygit, vite, pm2 and nats-server (5 of 20) are 0 of 20 after; through the real analyzers a bash function under a ruled comment block gets 'Safe field extraction from JSON on stdin.', and a Go struct under a bare block opener gets its sentence. Tests: test_doc_comment_summary.py (13 comment syntaxes x 10 shapes) and test_doc_comment_summary_e2e.py (bash, Go, JavaScript, C). ACCEPTANCE COUNT (count_docstrings.py, the same twelve repositories re-surveyed): summaries with no letters, a shebang, an encoding line or a licence line, 113 of 14,518 before (Go, JavaScript, TypeScript, Elm, Rust, shell), 0 of 14,493 after. RESIDUAL filed: WI-bojuz-bovuj-ninip-nasok-mosud-dokuk-hidij-babit (a lint pragma as a summary). Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/outside_reader_review2_11142026 (results.txt before, results_after.txt after; 20 repositories that are not hypergumbo, re-surveyed on the PR branch before its last two sketch commits, which were checked by direct calls). "  # 34e1
